  "bio": {
    "eyebrow": "About Antonio Kim",
    "heading_lead": "Meet",
    "heading_warm": "Antonio Kim.",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Antonio Kim (Kyung Ho Kim) is a Registered Physiotherapist (ABN: 82 277 933 512) (PHY0001355000) consulting at the Earlwood centre.",
      "He holds a Bachelor of Applied Science in Physiotherapy and brings extensive clinical experience practicing across both private clinics and specialized aged care facilities, where he has focused heavily on upgrading the physical health and quality of life for elderly residents.",
      "Antonio has a proven track record of supporting diverse sports teams with on-field acute care, strapping, and physical rehabilitation. His comprehensive clinical practice covers a wide spectrum of musculoskeletal and corporate conditions, including acute sporting injuries, postural dysfunctions, complex neck and back pain, tendonitis, work-related occupational injuries, and pre- and post-operative knee reconstructions.",
      "He takes an active, evidence-based approach to patient care, combining targeted manual therapies with customized exercise prescription to facilitate long-term recovery. Antonio is a member of the Australian Physiotherapy Association (APA), Musculoskeletal Physiotherapy Australia (MPA), and Sports Physiotherapy Australia (SPA)."
    ]
  },
